+ * are doubles exactly (53-bit significands, in double's normal range) rounds as IEEE double arithmetic does, so the
+ * host's double result, when it is normal and away from double's range edges, is softfloat's floatx80 result bit for
+ * bit; anything else (zeros, other precisions or modes, wider significands, edges) takes softfloat.  QEMU 5.0 merges
+ * no softfloat exception flag into the status word, so the value is all an op leaves.
